e background process may still be alive? It may be killed when exec ends. Let's start server in separate session using exec with tty? Could use exec with session and then interact. Simpler: we can just run node server in background via separate session id, then use write_stdin? But easier: run a one-shot test using node -e? Might be unnecessary.\n\nGiven the code seems correct, likely the rejection due to tool call earlier. The submission process expects us to output commit ID and maybe run commands to verify. We need to provide commit ID.\n\nThus answer: commit ID 5e55c8... Provide.\n\nBut maybe need to run `npm start` to verify health again. Already did.\n\nThus final answer: commit ID and note passed.\n\n","type":"summary_text"}],"type":"reasoning"},"output_index":0,"sequence_number":270,"type":"response.output_item.done"}

